KG42.register("rules-470f0b82b78a4e7ccb2a101a",{"id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R004","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R004","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01-p2p-cda","name":"Local market coordinator","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"Demand bids arrive asynchronously at the community exchange. Scope: P2P community exchange during the CDA Agreement Period, for time slots in Target Time Period T. Supply asks arrive asynchronously at the community exchange. Scope: P2P community exchange during the CDA Agreement Period, for time slots in Target Time Period T.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.local_operator under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand","bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E07"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E07"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"P2P community exchange during the CDA Agreement Period, for time slots in Target Time Period T.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E07"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Demand bids arrive asynchronously at the community exchange. Scope: P2P community exchange during the CDA Agreement Period, for time slots in Target Time Period T.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E07"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Supply asks arrive asynchronously at the community exchange. Scope: P2P community exchange during the CDA Agreement Period, for time slots in Target Time Period T.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E07"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E05","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 2. The timeline for ancillary service provision As presented in Section 2, customers trade ener","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A bid, which is submitted by a buyer, is represented by o_{b,t}(b_t, π_{b,t}, σ_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}), which means that the buyer b_t would like to by the σ_{b,t} (kWh) amount of electricity at the price π_{b,t} (£/kWh), and the bid arrives at the ‘exchange’ at the time τ_{b,t}. Note that the exchange is a centralized or decentralized platform set for P2P energy trading within the community. Similarly, an ask, which is submitted by a seller is represented by o_{s,t}(s_t, π_{s,t}, σ_{s,t}, τ_{s,t})."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E06","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"peach time slot t in the Target Time Period T, there is one order book. In seeach order book, the bi","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Within the Agreement Period of CDA, bids and asks will arrive at the exchange asynchronously. After they arrive, the bids and asks are allocated in ‘order books’. Note that for the bids and asks associated with each time slot t in the Target Time Period T, there is one order book. In each order book, the bids are sorted in the descending order of the bid prices π_{b,t} and the asks are sorted in the ascending order of the ask prices π_{s,t}. For both bids and asks, if several ones have the same prices, they are sorted based on the arrival time - the later a bid/ask arrives, the lower it ranks."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E07","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"peach time slot t in the Target Time Period T, there is one order book. In seeach order book, the bi","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Every time a bid/ask arrives at the exchange, it will be allocated in the corresponding order book based on the above-described principles, and then the exchange will try to match the bids and asks in the order book. If the following relationship is satisfied for a bid o_{b,t} and an ask o_{s,t}: π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t}, (1) then the following amount of electricity will be matched: σ_{matched,t} = min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t}) (2)"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No design-selection or operational decision variable is declared by these arrival constraints. The only related quantities, tau_{b,t} and tau_{s,t}, are order arrival-time descriptors defined in E05; this rule states only that arrivals are asynchronous, without a quantitative decision over them, and no domain for them is supplied within this rule scope.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed coefficient, bound, price, or exogenous constant is defined by C001/C002. The exchange platform and asynchronous arrival are procedural; no parameter value is supplied. The arrival-time descriptors tau_{b,t} and tau_{s,t} are not treated as parameters here because the source does not give a distribution, bounds, or a formula using them in this rule."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-matching"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.local_operator","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E06","quote":"Within the Agreement Period of CDA, bids and asks will arrive at the exchange asynchronously."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E05","quote":"Note that the exchange is a centralized or decentralized platform set for P2P energy trading within the community."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E07","quote":"the exchange will try to match the bids and asks in the order book."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E06","quote":"Within the Agreement Period of CDA, bids and asks will arrive at the exchange asynchronously."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E05","quote":"Note that the exchange is a centralized or decentralized platform set for P2P energy trading within the community."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E07","quote":"the exchange will try to match the bids and asks in the order book."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"d35ee2cd411a0de4fa920d80342b0d59f4ce86546142f209124c8202155ea76c","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen constraints C001 and C002 are procedural arrival conditions: demand bids and supply asks arrive asynchronously at the community exchange. The supplied source text provides no equation, decision variable, or fixed parameter for this rule; the order arrival times tau_{b,t} and tau_{s,t} appear only as descriptors in the bid/ask objects (v141-b-g01-E05) and are not quantitatively constrained here. Matching quantities and prices are formalized under other rules, not this coordinator rule. Therefore this rule is non-mathematical, and x/theta are empty for source-specific reasons rather than because extraction failed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","node_ids":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"C001 records the procedural arrival of demand bids at the exchange/coordinator; frozen edge E001 links bidding.demand to coordination.local_operator under this constraint."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","node_ids":["bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E002"],"rationale":"C002 records the procedural arrival of supply asks at the exchange/coordinator; frozen edge E002 links bidding.supply to coordination.local_operator under this constraint."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
